# Test: ze doctor refuses to call a config ready when the BGP engine rejects it
# VALIDATES: checkBGPPeerConfig (internal/component/doctor/checks_config.go) is
#            WIRED into runChecks -- an engine-invalid peer config produces the
#            doctor-config-bgp-peer diagnostic, ready=false, and exit 1.
# PREVENTS:  the operator trap this check exists to close. Before it, `ze doctor`
#            reported "ready": true and exited 0 for a config `ze config
#            validate` rejects and the daemon refuses to start on.
#
# This is the WIRING test. The unit tests
# (internal/component/doctor/checks_config_bgp_peer_test.go) call
# checkBGPPeerConfig directly, so deleting its one call site in doctor.go left
# every one of them green -- exactly the gap ai/rules/integration-completeness.md
# calls BLOCKING and never deferrable. Only this file fails if the append at
# doctor.go goes away.
#
# The fault is a missing `prefix { maximum }`, which PeersFromConfigTree reports
# as "prefix maximum is mandatory and must be > 0". Any engine rejection works;
# this one is the cheapest to express and is the same defect two shipped test
# fixtures (test/ui/doctor-bgp-listen.ci, doctor-bgp-md5.ci) were carrying
# unnoticed.

tmpfs=bad-peer.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
    router-id 1.2.3.4
    session {
        asn {
            local 65000
        }
    }
    peer peer1 {
        connection {
            local {
                ip 127.0.0.1
            }
            remote {
                ip 192.0.2.1
            }
        }
        session {
            asn {
                remote 65001
            }
            family {
                ipv4/unicast {
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json bad-peer.conf:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-config-bgp-peer
expect=stdout:contains=prefix maximum is mandatory
expect=stdout:contains="ready": false
